    Take that step with `Stream_Prod.send_Msg_Prod_Cons_1` first.
    This state is the top of protocol `Stream`'s `loop`, where a branch that repeats comes back to. To go round again, pass the state to a function that takes it as a parameter (usually `Prod`'s own function, called again) instead of closing.
    The conversation so far, in protocol `Stream`:

      loop do                   (repeats)
        Prod -> Cons : Int      <- `Prod` must do this next
        choose by Cons: done    other branch: `more`
          Cons -> Prod : Bool
          stop                  <- `Prod` tried to close here

    `Prod` is here: it must send an `Int` to `Cons`:

8 |       Prod -> Cons : Int
          ^^^^

